-- every build in the three lists is a legal one --
  120 of them
-- and nothing outside the lists is --
  nobody has ever been a wizard
  the summoning does not make bards
  custard is not an element that answers
-- an origin is stats and a rule; a calling is only a kit --
  librarian  MIG 3  FOC 4  GRI 3  WIT 5   Read the Room: you can see what a thing is made of before you touch it
  soldier    MIG 5  FOC 3  GRI 4  WIT 3   Drilled: the first thing you do on a floor costs you nothing
  nurse      MIG 3  FOC 5  GRI 3  WIT 4   Triage: when you mend, you also clear one condition
  chef       MIG 4  FOC 3  GRI 5  WIT 3   Mise en Place: what you carry works twice as well and never costs a turn
  programmer MIG 3  FOC 4  GRI 3  WIT 5   Rubber Duck: once a floor, you may take back a resolution and choose again
-- a mage gets the whole element, everybody else gets the first of it --
  knight  Guard, Shield Bash, Riposte, Hold the Line, Chill
  mage    Dispel, Read Aether, Chill, Rime
  ranger  Loose, Snare, Scout, Volley, Chill
  cleric  Mend, Ward, Smite, Consecrate, Chill
-- and the third tier waits on the world --
  locked:   4 arts, and Deepfreeze is not one of them
  at 10:     5 arts, including Deepfreeze
-- every affinity is soft to its opposite --
  fire   -> soft to frost
  frost  -> soft to fire
  storm  -> soft to earth
  earth  -> soft to storm
  light  -> soft to void
  void   -> soft to light

-- the material rules: what a thing is made of --
      rule                                         fires   else
   1. armoured halves anything but storm and light   2  vs    5
   2. a swarm takes half from a single strike        2  vs    5
   2.   and double from anything that covers the room  30  vs   15
   3. fire doubles against the frost-blooded        10  vs    5
   4. frost doubles against the wet                  8  vs    4
   5. storm doubles against armour instead of halving  10  vs    5
   6. earth cannot reach anything flying             0  vs    6
   7. light triples against the undead              12  vs    4
   8. fire does nothing to the ember-blooded         0  vs    5

-- the ground rules: where you are standing --
      rule                                         fires   else
   9. fire on gas takes the whole room              10  vs    5
   9.   and a good deal of you with it               6  vs    0
  10. fire on damp is half wasted boiling it         2  vs    5
  12. frost on damp freezes the floor over           4  vs    4
  14. storm on metal comes back up your arm          1  vs    0
  15. storm in a narrow room has nowhere else to be   4  vs    0
  18. wind thins anything that has to travel         3  vs    5

-- the rules that change the room rather than the numbers --
  fire on damp leaves:            dark
  frost on damp leaves:           slick
  light on dark leaves:              (and asks: revealed)
  fire on gas leaves:             burning   (and asks: ignition)
  earth in a narrow room asks:    collapse
  fire on sacred costs:           corruption 2
  void always costs:              corruption 1, and mp goes 16 -> 16 despite the cost

-- resonance is the only thing an affinity is for --
  in tune:      resonance 1
  out of tune:  resonance 0
-- and striking something that cannot answer is noticed --
  corruption 1

-- the outcomes nobody wrote down --
  fire into a gas-filled chapel:  10 done, 6 taken, corruption 2, and it still asks ignition
  fire at an armoured frost-thing, in water:
     half for the water, half for the plate, double for the cold: 2
     and the cold is gone afterwards: fax
  storm into a narrow flooded room: 5 done, 4 taken -- the water includes you
  storm down the iron gallery:     25 across 3 of them, 1 back

-- the cascade: what the room does once you have changed it --
  a frost mage in a burning room takes 6 (their own opposite, doubled)
  and the thing in it stops being frost-blooded: fax
  and the gas goes: burning
  slick ground trips what stands on it: stumbling
  a swarm cut in half becomes two of itself: 2 of them

-- the preview and the outcome are the same call --
  252 rooms, 0 that resolved differently the second time
-- and resolving never touches the state it was handed --
  identical afterwards: fax

